## T11 — Identity fencing and session-end hold
Reasoning: Shared-browser and account-switch safety (R1-q16 A) is its own guarantee across all tabs.
Task: Before every dispatch and fence the authenticated application user must equal the item owner; an identity change 
or sign-out in any tab stops drains in all tabs; late create/fence/lookup responses after a switch, or 
older-generation/cancelled-item responses under the same identity, are discarded without changing any view, item, or 
claim; items are held only when the client auth state reports the session ended and drain after the same user signs in 
again; another user never sees, sends, or deletes them; a 401 with a valid client session stays transient.
Done when: AC-012, AC-044 (client clauses), and AC-047 (switch and same-identity clauses) hold in the real UI.
Verify by: New E2E specs (session cleared/refresh revoked then C signs in, paused drain then switch to C, held real 
create/fence responses released after switch, cancel, or supersede) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; 
regression suites pass.
Covers: FR-011, FR-012, BR-001, AC-012, AC-044, AC-047
Root: T11
Depends on: T9

## T12 — Sign-out confirmation with unsent messages
Reasoning: User-initiated sign-out deletes the outbox; touches the Presence logout path, so it is isolated.
Task: At every reachable in-app sign-out control (today `EnhancedUserMenu`; any other found when the task starts is 
included), with N > 0 unsent items a dialog shows "Você tem N mensagens não enviadas. Sair apaga essas mensagens." 
with "Sair mesmo"/"Cancelar" (focus-trapped, Esc = Cancelar); Cancelar has no logout request, notice, or navigation; 
Sair mesmo stops drains in all tabs, deletes the user's outbox, and runs the existing sign-out with the Presence 
logout sequence unchanged; with N = 0 sign-out is unchanged.
Done when: AC-013 and the AC-047 Sair-mesmo clause hold for every reachable sign-out control, and the dialog is 
keyboard-operable.
Verify by: New E2E spec (each reachable control enumerated in TRACK, a drain in flight in another tab, held responses 
after Sair mesmo, re-login with empty outbox, keyboard operation) passes 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; 
Presence E2E logout tests pass; presence-safety review recorded.
Covers: FR-013, BR-008, AC-013, AC-037, AC-047
Root: T12
Depends on: T11

