36: ## T7 — Client correlation by clientMessageId
37: Reasoning: Every pending/stored match in the outbox and across tabs depends on key-based correlation; it is 
observable on its own (AC-050).
38: Task: The sender's representations of a message (create/fence responses — already carrying it since T2 —, feed 
fetches via the repository mapper, Realtime events — whose INSERT payload already has `client_message_id` —, 
optimistic items) carry `clientMessageId`; the feed matches pending items to stored messages only by that key in every 
sender tab.
39: Done when: AC-050 holds: identical texts (one plain, one reply) with Realtime arriving before HTTP show as exactly 
one bubble each in both of A's tabs throughout.
40: Verify by: New E2E spec for AC-050 passes 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
41: Covers: FR-034, AC-050
42: Root: T7
43: Depends on: T2, T24
