45: ## T8 — Durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery
46: Reasoning: The core of G1: write-before-dispatch, persistence across reload/close, ordered automatic drain meeting 
D1; unknown-outcome recovery follows in T27.
47: Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, reply 
target, requested mention IDs, original send time, window start, order, state, generation) before dispatch and before 
the composer clears; pending items render with a text label; items drain automatically per conversation in order when 
connectivity returns, with ≤ 10 pending and quota available all delivered within 10 s; confirmed items become the 
normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); 
if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 
message.
48: Done when: AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, and AC-039 hold in the real UI, and 10 messages queued offline are 
delivered in order, once each, within 10 s of reconnecting.
49: Verify by: New E2E specs for those ACs plus the 10-message D1 timing case (offline context, reload offline, tab 
close, IndexedDB disabled and failing writes) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
50: Covers: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003, FR-010, FR-033, BR-002, BR-003, AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, AC-039
51: Root: T8
52: Depends on: T7
