72: ## T9 — Definitive failures, rate-limit retry, and expiry
73: Reasoning: The user-visible failure states (BR-005 definitive, 429 transient, BR-006 expiry) are a separate 
outcome from unknown recovery.
74: Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only later 
items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under a new 
key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry automatically in order; items fenced as not stored 24 
h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not stored" — 
T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the original send time and opens a new 24 h window under the 
normal rules.
75: Done when: AC-007, AC-008, AC-009 (drawer clause), AC-010, AC-043, and the AC-046 definitive-class clauses hold, 
and an expired item retried manually keeps its original send time in the outbox.
76: Verify by: New E2E specs (removed room access via T24 re-add fixture, local quota exhaustion with 12 items, 
